  Tīriyeremandu ‘Toda ti: dairy-temple, hence the name of numerous abandoned Toda hamlets, of which twelve can be identified: 1. Tiriyaramund, Teriyaramund, Tîmad, Timog, Toda Christian Colony, a long-abandoned ti: dairy of Kaṣ clan, 5.5 km. SW of Ootacamund (0.8 ha in 1893; since 1913 occupied by Toda Christians); 2. Thiriyar mund, Kundathiriyaraimund, a ti: dairy 11.5 km. WSW of Ootacamund (abandoned in the 19th Cent.; also called Kunda Ti:riyeremandu );, 3. Tiriyarimund, Teriyaramund, Theriyeri-mund, Tiriyeremand, Timarimund, Mudimund, Katedva, a ti: dairy of No'ṣṣ clan, 18 km. W of Ootacamund ; 4. Tiriaraimund, Theraimund, Tevar-mund, Mòdr, Mory, a ti: dairy of No'ṣ clan 12 km. WNW of Ootacamund ; 5. Tiriyaraimund, Òdrtho, Or8öw, a ti: dairy of Nøo'ṣ clan 13 km. WNW of Ootacamund ; 6. Kombutukkimand, Kombutukkimund, Koduthukimund, Kombuthkimund, Koobuntaky, Kudòdr, Kudòdrs, Kudop ti, a ti: dairy of Mör clan name of a Toda hamlet of Noṣ clan 5.5 km. WNW of Ootacamund ; 7. Poș, Posh, a ti: dairy 10 km. NW of Ootacamund (adjoining Kengo:dumandu); 8. Anto, Ontöw, a ti: dairy of No'ṣ clan, 7.5 km. NNW of Ootacamund ; 9. Tarzhva, Tarsòdr, Tazòdr, Taso, Selykasḍi, a ti: dairy of Mör clan, 27.5 km. SW of Ootacamund ; 10. Kammundthiriveramund, Lingmand, Kòn, a ti; dairy of Ka's clan located in the Kunde region, “about two miles” from Tarzhva, Tarsòdr, Tazòdr, Taso, Selykasḍi, 28 km. SW of Ootacamund ; 11. a ti: dairy was once located SE of Ootacamund, near Ke:ti (location uncertain; 8.1 ha land in 1893); 12. Theriyeru-mund, Pursâs, Pisas, a ti: dairy of Pïirgor clan, 11.5 km. NNE of Kotagiri (12.3 ha. in 1893; also called Ko:gdana:dumandu, q.v., abandoned early in the 20th Cent.; Rivers 1906:121; Emeneau 1971: xlii-xliii; “there are about nineteen Tiriaris occupied at’ noun proper-noun uncertain   IDs=f_rufmcae6mmere SRC=hockings-pilotraichoor1992[p. 293, col. 1]
  Tīriyere Beṭṭu ‘Thiriyerabettu, Thiriyara-bettu, Theriyerebettu, name of three mountains: 1. is ca 2330 m in elevation, 27.5 km. SW of Ootacamund; 2. is ca 2370 m in elevation, 26 km. SW of Ootacamund; 3. is ca 2200 m in elevation, 26 km. SSW of Ootacamund, on the border with Malappuram District, Kerala (each stood above a Ti:riyeremandu, q.V.; < ti:ri+(y)ere+ettu, ‘dairy-temple+ temporary shed+tmountain’)’ noun proper-noun uncertain   IDs=f_u74pugdru324w SRC=hockings-pilotraichoor1992[p. 293, col. 1]
  ere ‘1. veranda, front room (where young couples and visitors from outside the community would sleep overnight; originally a loose structure of bamboo with a woven bamboo door; along the whole line of houses which includes the dogda mane of a hamlet, there should be no ere except at the two end houses; this is to allow more room for participants in any ceremony at’ noun uncertain   IDs=f_uoy6j3ls2g3rg SRC=hockings-pilotraichoor1992[p. 87, col. 2]
